.TH MOONGLOW 1 "October 2026" "moonglow 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moonglow \- external-display brightness and scheduled colour temperature
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moonglow
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Moonglow drives external-monitor brightness over DDC/CI and
follows a morning/evening colour-temperature schedule. The first invocation
starts the application; later invocations forward commands to the running
instance. With no daemon running, the setter flags drive the hardware directly
and exit, which suits headless use and scripts.
.PP
The settings window has brightness and colour-temperature sliders, a day/night
range, and global shortcuts. Closing the window keeps the app running in the
background so the schedule and shortcuts stay active.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-show\-settings
Show the settings window.
.TP
.BR \-\-quit
Quit the running instance.
.TP
.BR \-\-set\-brightness " " \fIPERCENT\fP
Set brightness 1\-100.
.TP
.BR \-\-brighter ", " \-\-dimmer
Step brightness by 5%.
.TP
.BR \-\-set\-temp " " \fIKELVIN\fP
Set colour temperature (manual mode).
.TP
.BR \-\-warmer ", " \-\-cooler
Step temperature by 100 K (manual mode).
.TP
.BR \-\-auto " " \fIon\fP|\fIoff\fP
Turn automatic temperature on or off.
.TP
.BR \-\-day\-temp ", " \-\-night\-temp " " \fIKELVIN\fP
Set the daytime / nighttime schedule target.
.TP
.BR \-\-morning ", " \-\-evening " " \fIFROM TO\fP
Set a transition window; times are 24h "HH:MM".
.TP
.BR \-\-login " " \fIon\fP|\fIoff\fP
Turn start-at-login on or off.
.TP
.BR \-\-status
Print brightness, temperature, schedule, and displays.
.TP
.BR \-\-status " " \-\-json
Machine-readable status.
.TP
.BR \-\-hidden
Start with the window hidden (used by the autostart entry).
.TP
.BR \-\-headless
Run schedule and shortcuts with no settings window.
.TP
.BR \-\-brightness\-up ", " \-\-brightness\-down
Global-shortcut action: step brightness by 5%.
.TP
.BR \-\-temperature\-up ", " \-\-temperature\-down
Global-shortcut action: step temperature by 100 K; turns automatic off first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/moonglow/moonglow.log
Diagnostics log (XDG state dir).
.TP
.I ~/.config/moonglow/settings.json
Persisted settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/moonglow.sock
Single-instance IPC socket.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/moonglow.desktop
Start-at-login entry, managed by the app.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/51-moonglow-i2c.rules
Gives the i2c group access to DDC/CI buses.
.SH DDC/CI ACCESS
Brightness needs i2c access: install i2c-tools, run
.B sudo usermod \-aG i2c $USER\fP,
then log out and back in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ddcutil (1),
.BR udev (7)
